{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-opg-37079-a-gold-grabbing-game-ab8996b2-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-opg-37079-a-gold-grabbing-game-ab8996b2-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-opg-37079-a-gold-grabbing-game-ab8996b2-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-37079-a-gold-grabbing-game-ab8996b2-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-37079"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Setup Fix a tree $T$ and for every vertex $v \\in V(T)$ a non-negative integer $g(v)$ which we think of as the amount of gold at $v$. 2-Player game Players alternate turns. On each turn, a player chooses a leaf vertex $v$ of the tree, takes the gold at this vertex, and then deletes $v$. The game ends when the tree is empty, and the winner is the player who has accumulated the most gold. Problem Find optimal strategies for the players."}, "statement_sha256": "3cf64def29c7dd93da9d062dc80a6af02c7176f5329ba9e1034eae4ef119cd0b"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-37079-a-gold-grabbing-game-ab8996b2-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-37079"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha2